From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander <4418484+kuscher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:48:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/14] Android: open and save documents through the system
 picker

Android hands out documents (content:// URIs), not paths. As the web build
does with the browser, the pickers copy the chosen document into a working
copy under the app's storage and return its path, so the path-based open
and save pipelines run unchanged; after a save the working copy is copied
back to its document. Each working copy sits beside a .uri file naming its
document, access is kept across restarts, and reopening a recent file
reads the document again first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
